// The screen-space blue-noise mask (D-095) — a void-and-cluster tile bound
// once in the scene descriptor set, beside the environment texture. Its one job
// is to key each pixel's Sobol sample-index permutation (rng.slang's
// blueRankedIndex), so that at low sample counts neighbouring pixels draw
// complementary strata and the ReSTIR estimate's Monte-Carlo error lands as
// blue noise across the frame — perceptually far cleaner than white noise at
// equal spp, and converging to the identical image.
//
// A renderer-global constant, not scene data: it rides the scene set only
// because that is the binding model's home for read-only sampling resources the
// reservoir stages share (the TLAS, the environment). Host side: generated by
// `src/bluenoise.rs`, uploaded once, written at binding 3.

import rng;

// The tile is TILE×TILE ranks in [0, TILE²), row-major (`y·TILE + x`), tiled
// toroidally over the frame — void-and-cluster wraps seamlessly, so the repeat
// is invisible. Mirrors `bluenoise::TILE`.
public static const uint BLUE_NOISE_TILE = 64;

[vk::binding(3, 0)]
StructuredBuffer<uint> blueNoiseMask;

// This pixel's blue-noise key: the mask value at its toroidally-tiled position.
public uint blueNoiseKey(uint2 coords) {
    let x = coords.x % BLUE_NOISE_TILE;
    let y = coords.y % BLUE_NOISE_TILE;
    return blueNoiseMask[y * BLUE_NOISE_TILE + x];
}

// The blue-noise-ranked sample index for this pixel and sample — the one call
// the reservoir stages make, folding the mask fetch and the ranking together.
// Shared across the sample's dimensions (see rng.slang's blueRankedIndex).
public uint blueRank(uint2 coords, uint sampleIndex) {
    return blueRankedIndex(blueNoiseKey(coords), sampleIndex);
}
